The page-scoped controller separates the raw filter draft, applied query, complete list observation and complete detail observation. It keeps visited cursor history, handles explicit apply/reset/retry/first-page actions, and treats cancellation as a stable error requiring explicit reread. Only a fresh instance may wait for an existing owner and then issue one initial default read. Checking, identity loss and disposal retire the old instance. A route-leave cancellation keeps a surviving instance subscribed and explicitly refreshable if a later guard prevents navigation; final disposal clears its state. These are controller checks, not claims that the future View lifecycle is wired or native focus is verified.

